                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "This is a fun little game that reminds me a lot of Majesty or Depths of Peril. I really like the feeling of building up a little town and conquering the world. It is strangely satisfying, even though the overall depth is lacking a bit here. You can set up a small, medium, or large world, the smallest only taking you a couple hours to beat, so this lets you finish in an evening or an afternoon and have a complete experience. I like the monster models, things from gnolls to dark elves, undead, giants, and even dragons are all here and you really do feel like you are going from zero to hero over the course of a map. You'll start with nothing but a rusty dagger and clothes and end up with high-end magical equipment. There are a lot of character class options which helps replayability.\r\nI do think that if this game had more map variety (snow, desert, lava, etc) and actual dungeons instead of just an overland map, it would take it from being pretty good to absolutely amazing.  Hopefully one day this will inspire a sequel, DLC, or a spiritual successor to really take this concept to its full potential.\r\nOverall I recommend this game. It's low stress, relatively quick to play, and gives you a good fantasy town/adventurer simulation in a neat little package.",
